          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: 当家",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "当家 — dāngjiā — \"to run the household\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "我们家是我妈妈当家 wǒmen jiā shì wǒ māma dāngjiā — In our family, it's my mum who runs things."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "当家 (dāngjiā) is built from 当 'to be in charge' and 家 'a home', both inherited from Middle Chinese, tang and kae (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first 'to be in charge' and the second 'a dwelling'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
